    {
      "type": "MarkdownNote",
      "pos": [
        0,
        210
      ],
      "size": [
        580,
        880
      ],
      "inputs": [],
      "outputs": [],
      "title": "Model Links",
      "properties": {},
      "widgets_values": [
        "## Kling Image → HDR Workflow for Radiance:\n\n1. Kling 3.0 Omni Image generates the image through ComfyUI's API nodes (sign in to your Comfy account; the run uses API credits). Edit the prompt and settings there.\n2. SDR → HDR Universal runs RUDRA ACES 2 (Auto, about 3 MB, downloaded on first run): a scene-linear master (1.0 = 203 nits) whose ACES 2.0 SDR view keeps the generated codes. reconstructed_mask marks where light was rebuilt.\n3. SDR → HDR AI Fill (RUDRA v3) is bypassed. Select it and press Ctrl+B to regenerate large blown highlights (needs Wan2.1-VACE-1.3B and a 16 GB GPU; downloaded on first use).\n4. The Viewer shows the master through ACES 2.0 against the SDR source: use the wipe to see what RUDRA rebuilt.\n5. Write EXR saves a 32-bit float EXR: the master as beauty and rudra.reconstructed as its own channel. Output: output/radiance_api/.\n\n- Radiance: [Documentation](https://www.fxtdstudios.com/comfyu-radiance-docs/)\n- Radiance: [GitHub](https://github.com/FXTD-Studios/radiance)\n\n## Radiance Report Issues :\nTo report any issues with Radiance nodes, [go to GitHub](https://github.com/FXTD-Studios/radiance/issues)\n\n## Model Links\n\nNo model to download: Kling Image runs through ComfyUI's API nodes (sign in to your Comfy account; each run uses API credits). RUDRA ACES 2 (about 3 MB) downloads itself into `ComfyUI/models/radiance` on the first run.\n\n## Report Issue\n\nNote: Please update ComfyUI first ([guide](https://docs.comfy.org/installation/update_comfyui)) and prepare required models. Desktop/Cloud updates follow stable releases, so some nightly-supported models may not be available yet.\n\n- Cannot run / runtime errors: [ComfyUI/issues](https://github.com/Comfy-Org/ComfyUI/issues)\n- UI / frontend issues: [ComfyUI_frontend/issues](https://github.com/Comfy-Org/ComfyUI_frontend/issues)"
      ],
      "widgets_values_named": {
        "text": "## Kling Image → HDR Workflow for Radiance:\n\n1. Kling 3.0 Omni Image generates the image through ComfyUI's API nodes (sign in to your Comfy account; the run uses API credits). Edit the prompt and settings there.\n2. SDR → HDR Universal runs RUDRA ACES 2 (Auto, about 3 MB, downloaded on first run): a scene-linear master (1.0 = 203 nits) whose ACES 2.0 SDR view keeps the generated codes. reconstructed_mask marks where light was rebuilt.\n3. SDR → HDR AI Fill (RUDRA v3) is bypassed. Select it and press Ctrl+B to regenerate large blown highlights (needs Wan2.1-VACE-1.3B and a 16 GB GPU; downloaded on first use).\n4. The Viewer shows the master through ACES 2.0 against the SDR source: use the wipe to see what RUDRA rebuilt.\n5. Write EXR saves a 32-bit float EXR: the master as beauty and rudra.reconstructed as its own channel. Output: output/radiance_api/.\n\n- Radiance: [Documentation](https://www.fxtdstudios.com/comfyu-radiance-docs/)\n- Radiance: [GitHub](https://github.com/FXTD-Studios/radiance)\n\n## Radiance Report Issues :\nTo report any issues with Radiance nodes, [go to GitHub](https://github.com/FXTD-Studios/radiance/issues)\n\n## Model Links\n\nNo model to download: Kling Image runs through ComfyUI's API nodes (sign in to your Comfy account; each run uses API credits). RUDRA ACES 2 (about 3 MB) downloads itself into `ComfyUI/models/radiance` on the first run.\n\n## Report Issue\n\nNote: Please update ComfyUI first ([guide](https://docs.comfy.org/installation/update_comfyui)) and prepare required models. Desktop/Cloud updates follow stable releases, so some nightly-supported models may not be available yet.\n\n- Cannot run / runtime errors: [ComfyUI/issues](https://github.com/Comfy-Org/ComfyUI/issues)\n- UI / frontend issues: [ComfyUI_frontend/issues](https://github.com/Comfy-Org/ComfyUI_frontend/issues)"
      },
